Create a complete 3D Maze Escape game using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript with Three.js. The requirements are:

1. Use Three.js to create a first-person maze environment with walls, floor, and ceiling.
2. Player should move using W, A, S, D keys (forward, left, back, right).
3. Add basic collision detection so the player cannot walk through walls.
4. Place a green cube as the exit point.
5. When the player reaches the exit, display a message “You Escaped the Maze!” on the screen.
6. Add ambient and point lighting for realistic effects.
7. The maze should be randomly generated or at least look complex.
8. Include detailed comments explaining each part of the code.
9. Make sure it runs correctly in Replit’s HTML, CSS, JS project setup.
10. Use minimal CSS and responsive full-screen canvas.

Title it “3D Maze Escape by Aditya”.
